{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "54c8c13b-bc09-8fca-9dfa-e77222807163",
  "created_at": "2025-12-19T12:12:49-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Carlos Amaral",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Denise Arruda",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:07:34-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Denise. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:07:39-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hello, good afternoon. My name is Carlos Amaral. I am calling about the road. The edge of the road is breaking apart, crumbling, at a curve near my house."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:07:53-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, I can take that down. Where is the curve? What's the address or the closest one?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:08:02-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It is in front of 479 Old Beach Road. By Easton's Beach side. The curve is just before my driveway, coming from the beach."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:08:14-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four seventy-nine Old Beach Road. Got it. And when you say crumbling, is it the pavement at the edge, like pieces coming off?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:08:25-05:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, exactly. The asphalt at the edge is coming off in pieces, small and some big. After the rain Wednesday and Thursday, yesterday it was finishing, it is more. There is now a bite out of the edge, like somebody took a bite."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:08:45-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, the wet weather does that, water gets under the edge and then it breaks up. How big is the missing piece, would you say?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:08:57-05:00",
      "duration": 26,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hmm. About, maybe, one meter long. And maybe from here to here, the width of my arm. Sorry, I am on the phone, you cannot see. Half a meter, I think. And it is right in the bike lane. That is what worries the people on the bicycles, because they go right on that part."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:09:23-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, so it's in the bike lane at the curve. That's helpful, I'll note that so it gets looked at with that in mind. Is there any loose gravel out in the lane too?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:09:39-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, some gravel. I swept a little this morning with the broom but it keeps coming. I called the Highway Department before, no, wait. I think it is the Highway Department who does this? Or is it the Parks?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:09:57-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're in the right place. Roads and potholes come through Public Works here. Parks is a separate group, they handle the grounds and the playgrounds and so on."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:10:11-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ah, okay, okay. Sorry. In Portugal we say Obras Públicas, so I mix them. Public Works, yes. Good."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:10:20-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem at all. Happens a lot. Let me get a phone number in case the crew has a question about where exactly it is."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:10:32-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. It is four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-seven-six."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:10:36-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-seven-six. And that's Carlos, C-A-R-L-O-S, Amaral?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:10:41-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, Amaral, A-M-A-R-A-L. Correct."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:10:44-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Great. I'm putting it in as a road edge breakup at the curve, in the bike lane, in front of 479 Old Beach Road. I'll send it over to the crew supervisor."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:10:59-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you. Can I ask, how long it takes usually, for the repair? One week, one month? I do not know how it works here."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:11:11-05:00",
      "duration": 22,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It really varies. After a storm like this one the crews have a long list, so it can be a few days or it can be a couple of weeks. Cold weather matters too, they sometimes do a temporary patch first and the proper repair later."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:11:33-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A temporary patch, okay. That is fine, if it is safe for the bicycles. The patch first, then the right one later, when it is warmer."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:11:46-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's how it often goes in winter, yes. If it gets worse, say a big piece breaks off or it's turning into a hazard in the road, call back and tell us so, and we can update the report."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:12:04-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, I will do that. Should I put something there, like a cone? I have one in the garage."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:12:13-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'd rather you stay out of the road. Just keep an eye on it from your side and let us know if it changes."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:12:25-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, yes, that is better. I stay on my side. Then that is all I need."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:12:33-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Alright, Mr. Amaral. Anything else I can help with today?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:12:38-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, that is everything. Thank you for your help. Have a good weekend."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-19T12:12:45-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too. Take care, bye now."
    }
  ],
